[10/08/2026 23:22] SteeL: # Phantom — Stealth Header Layer for instagrapi

Phantom is a drop-in wrapper around [instagrapi](https://github.com/subzeroid/instagrapi).
It does not reimplement Instagram's API — it subclasses instagrapi.Client and layers
realistic request headers, navigation breadcrumbs, and endpoint metadata on top so the traffic
looks like the official Android app. All of instagrapi's methods (media_info, user_info_by_username,
media_like, media_comment, ...) work unchanged.

> Requires instagrapi. from phantom import EnhancedClient will fail without it installed.

---

## Installation

pip install instagrapi
# phantom lives in the `phantom/` directory of this repo — add the repo root to your path,
# or copy the `phantom/` folder into your project.

---

## Quick start

from phantom import EnhancedClient

client = EnhancedClient(debug=True)          # debug=True logs every added header
client.load_settings("session.json")          # path to a saved Instagram session

media = client.media_info(3921072280461367322)          # works exactly like instagrapi
user  = client.user_info_by_username("instagram")
client.media_like(media.id)
client.media_comment(media.id, "Great post!")

Every request automatically includes:

- Realistic app headers (User-Agent, X-IG-*, device metadata) via HeaderBuilder
- Navigation breadcrumbs (x-ig-nav-chain) via NavigationTracker

---

## Sessions & login

### 1. Load a saved session (recommended)

client = EnhancedClient()
client.load_settings("session.json")          # dump with client.dump_settings("session.json")

### 2. Login with username/password (Bloks CAA flow, with TFA support)

from phantom import EnhancedClient, login

client = EnhancedClient()
ok = login(client, "my_username", "my_password")            # returns True on success
# 2FA / OTP:
ok = login(client, "my_username", "my_password", verification_code="123456")
# Force re-login even when a session exists:
ok = login(client, "my_username", "my_password", relogin=True)

client.dump_settings("session.json")          # persist for next time

The raw flow is also available as phantom.login.LoginFlow(client).
